{"id":"22ec8272f07ee0fb","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy.md","title":"Woodin Cardinal Hierarchy","display":"thm-wcodin-hierarchy — Woodin Cardinal Hierarchy","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy","aliases":["58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy"],"display":"thm-wcodin-hierarchy — Woodin Cardinal Hierarchy","depends_on":["[[58-df-woodin]]","[[58-df-cardinal]]","[[58-df-inaccessible]]","[[58-df-class-elementary-embedding]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-wcodin-hierarchy — Woodin Cardinal Hierarchy"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"da3159c0c219916e\" href=\"?note=da3159c0c219916e\" title=\"58-df-woodin\">58-df-woodin</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5fb1c2241d1943d1\" href=\"?note=5fb1c2241d1943d1\" title=\"58-df-cardinal\">58-df-cardinal</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"06ee5d7ff126e916\" href=\"?note=06ee5d7ff126e916\" title=\"58-df-inaccessible\">58-df-inaccessible</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0fc577c79c699e0c\" href=\"?note=0fc577c79c699e0c\" title=\"58-df-class-elementary-embedding\">58-df-class-elementary-embedding</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta,A\\in V,\\quad A\\subseteq V_\\delta\">\\(\\delta,A\\in V,\\quad A\\subseteq V_\\delta\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Woodin},\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Woodin},\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}^3,\\quad\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}\">\\(\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}^3,\\quad\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}woodin\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash \\mathrm{Woodin}(\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\delta)\\land\\forall A\\subseteq V_\\delta\\;\\exists\\kappa\\in\\delta\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\delta\\;\\left(\\kappa&lt;\\lambda\\to\\exists M,j\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\left(\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}(M)\\land\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S(j,V,M)\\land j(\\kappa)\\neq\\kappa\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;(j(\\alpha)=\\alpha)\\land\\lambda&lt;j(\\kappa)\\land V_\\lambda\\subseteq M\\land j(A)\\cap V_\\lambda=A\\cap V_\\lambda\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}woodin\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash \\mathrm{Woodin}(\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\delta)\\land\\forall A\\subseteq V_\\delta\\;\\exists\\kappa\\in\\delta\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\delta\\;\\left(\\kappa&lt;\\lambda\\to\\exists M,j\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\left(\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}(M)\\land\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S(j,V,M)\\land j(\\kappa)\\neq\\kappa\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;(j(\\alpha)=\\alpha)\\land\\lambda&lt;j(\\kappa)\\land V_\\lambda\\subseteq M\\land j(A)\\cap V_\\lambda=A\\cap V_\\lambda\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This is the characterization saying that every <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq V_\\delta\">\\(A\\subseteq V_\\delta\\)</span> has a <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"&lt;\\delta\">\\(&lt;\\delta\\)</span>-strongness point below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\delta\">\\(\\delta\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The existence of a supercompact cardinal has greater consistency strength than the existence of a Woodin cardinal.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-woodin","status":"resolved","id":"da3159c0c219916e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-woodin]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-cardinal","status":"resolved","id":"5fb1c2241d1943d1","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-cardinal]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-inaccessible","status":"resolved","id":"06ee5d7ff126e916","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-inaccessible]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-class-elementary-embedding","status":"resolved","id":"0fc577c79c699e0c","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-class-elementary-embedding]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\delta,A\\in V,\\quad A\\subseteq V_\\delta","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Woodin},\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S:V\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}^3,\\quad\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}\\subseteq\\mathsf{Cls}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}woodin\\text{-}hierarchy} \\vdash \\mathrm{Woodin}(\\delta)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\delta)\\land\\forall A\\subseteq V_\\delta\\;\\exists\\kappa\\in\\delta\\;\\forall\\lambda\\in\\delta\\;\\left(\\kappa<\\lambda\\to\\exists M,j\\in\\mathsf{Cls}\\;\\left(\\operatorname{TransitiveClass}(M)\\land\\operatorname{ElementaryClassEmbedding}^{\\mathrm{sch}}_S(j,V,M)\\land j(\\kappa)\\neq\\kappa\\land\\forall\\alpha\\in\\kappa\\;(j(\\alpha)=\\alpha)\\land\\lambda<j(\\kappa)\\land V_\\lambda\\subseteq M\\land j(A)\\cap V_\\lambda=A\\cap V_\\lambda\\right)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"A\\subseteq V_\\delta","display":false},{"tex":"<\\delta","display":false},{"tex":"\\delta","display":false}],"bytes":1478,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4483","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy.md|58-thm-wcodin-hierarchy]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["da3159c0c219916e","5fb1c2241d1943d1","06ee5d7ff126e916","0fc577c79c699e0c"]}